From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 03:07:05 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 110/161] hjviewer: the PC's connection window shows the mark,
 a caution and recording (TV-W2 Dart)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

TV-W2: Client.fromJson reads hjv_mark only when it is a map of strings,
and hjv_recording only when it is true (hjvReadMark, hjvReadRecording), so
a 1.8.x core reads as no mark. add_connection copies the mark and the
recording state onto a card it sends again. The CM header draws the mark
line under the name in the kind's fixed icon and colour (same-account: the
shield; unverified-name: the warning sign; nothing for "" or an unknown
kind). The accept card shows the caution box while !authorized and the kind
is neither same-account nor staff (D-7), with 'HJViewer 관리자: <contact>'
from main_get_common("hjv-admin-contact"); P2 and P3 show it every time
(P3 in critic 2-5's words). A connected card shows the 'Recording' chip
and the line on how to stop it. When recording starts, the 3 s minimize is
cancelled and skipped while a peer records, and a minimized window comes
up on that card at most once a minute per connection (D-8).
New files: hjviewer_cm_texts.dart (texts and the pure rules),
hjv_admin_contact.dart (hjvAdminContact, HjvCautionBox) and
test/hjviewer_cm_test.dart; cm_demo.dart's guests carry the new values.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
